Execute Phase 5 only.

Use the verified Ollama connection for:
- Angles.
- Scripts.
- Storyboards.
- Ad concepts.
- Transcript-based clip analysis.

MODEL REGISTRY
Store configurable:
- Exact provider model ID.
- Availability.
- Supported/tested capabilities.
- Input/output limits.
- Cost-rate version.
- Last successful check.

Routing must be configurable and evaluation-based.
Do not claim one model is best from its name alone.

Use one model per task by default.
Do not call all six for every request.

JSON OUTPUT
Do not assume Ollama Cloud schema enforcement.
Request JSON in prompts.
Parse and independently validate.
Allow at most one disclosed repair attempt initially.
No unlimited repair loops.

PROPOSALS
Separate proposals from accepted content.
Respect locks.
Reject stale results.
Ignore late canceled responses.
Preserve history before replacement.

FACTUAL MODE
Use supplied source excerpts.
Map claims to source IDs and exact supporting excerpts.
Flag unsupported claims.
Review hooks/endings too.
Do not convert neutral acknowledgment into proof.

Insufficient evidence produces planning notes, not
a falsely complete sourced script.

STORYBOARD
Preserve script wording/order.
Allocate valid durations.
Never invent media IDs.

ACCEPTANCE
Real in-app factual and fiction generation can be reviewed,
accepted, saved, and reopened.

Stop after Phase 5.
